<article class="env-lemma" id="045B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/045B">Lemma <span data-tag="045B">94.10.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $\mathcal{X}$, $\mathcal{Y}$, $\mathcal{Z}$ be categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property as in Definition <a href="/tag/03YK" data-tag="03YK">94.10.1</a> which is stable under composition. Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$, $g : \mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ be $1$-morphisms which are representable by algebraic spaces. If $f$ and $g$ have property $\mathcal{P}$ so does $g \circ f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Z}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that the lemma makes sense by Lemma <a href="/tag/0301" data-tag="0301">94.9.9</a>. Proof omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>